{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqb1i22nzvv","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"Learned context gate is regularized logistic regression first, neural net only at volume","summary":"Architecture decision (2026-06-12) for the learned context gate. Stage A = L2-regularized logistic regression over the ~14 engineered journal features (NOT a deep net): at 200-500 labeled rows a real net overfits; LR is the bias-variance sweet spot. Three reasons LR is not a downgrade but the product enabler: (1) fits cleanly at hundreds of examples vs 10-100x more for a net; (2) coefficients are inspectable — read which feature drives inject, cross-check vs the rule guards; (3) per-repo adaptation = Platt recalibration of 2 params (A,B) on the logit, robust at n=20 local outcomes — THIS is what makes 'learns your repo in a day' real; a net has nothing this clean at n=20. Add sign-constrained monotone priors (higher cosine never lowers p(inject)) + ~3-4 hand-picked interaction terms (cosine x kbSize, gap x cluster) since a 0.55 cosine means different things in a 12-note vs 300-note KB. Stage B = graduate to GBT / small MLP only at thousands of rows. The rule floor (lib/context-gate.js 4-guard gateTask) NEVER goes away — it is the fallback when no model is present or embedModel drifts. Extends [[note-mqaslontp50]] [[note-mqatnwimnk0]].","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-12T14:46:40.895Z","vec":[0.0169401615858078,-0.1140657514333725,0.009587202221155167,0.020664332434535027,0.06569627672433853,-0.03415893390774727,0.03507906198501587,-0.05488204583525658,-0.025639718398451805,0.008003021590411663,0.02000979147851467,0.005684343166649342,-0.028345465660095215,0.043788209557533264,-0.04529657959938049,0.032528337091207504,-0.005053364671766758,0.040324896574020386,-0.13310953974723816,-0.03240140154957771,-0.03290531039237976,0.13088996708393097,0.07239065319299698,0.009674757719039917,0.017823437228798866,-0.007593151181936264,0.018204374238848686,0.0693703293800354,